Perfect 💪 — you want to create an **Angular directive** that automatically converts all the text inside an element to **uppercase** (changes lowercase → uppercase).  

Let’s create this cleanly, step by step 👇

---

## ✅ Step 1: Create a directive file

In your terminal, inside your Angular project folder, run:

```bash
ng g d directives/uppercase
```

This will create:
```
src/app/directives/uppercase.directive.ts
```
and automatically update your `app.module.ts`.

---

## ✅ Step 2: Update the directive code

Open the new file `uppercase.directive.ts` and replace everything with this:

```typescript
import { Directive, ElementRef, AfterViewInit } from '@angular/core';

@Directive({
  selector: '[appUppercase]'
})
export class UppercaseDirective implements AfterViewInit {
  constructor(private el: ElementRef) {}

  ngAfterViewInit() {
    const text = this.el.nativeElement.innerText;
    this.el.nativeElement.innerText = text.toUpperCase();

    console.log('UppercaseDirective works — text converted to UPPERCASE');
  }
}
```

---

## 🧠 How it works

- `ElementRef` gives access to the element the directive is attached to.
- `ngAfterViewInit()` runs after Angular renders the element.
- It reads the current `innerText`,
  converts it with `.toUpperCase()`,
  and puts it back.
- Logs `"UppercaseDirective works — text converted to UPPERCASE"` in the console ✅

---

## ✅ Step 3: Use it in your HTML

Example:
```html
<p appUppercase>This text will become uppercase automatically.</p>

<h2 appUppercase>login successful</h2>
```

💥 Output in the browser:
```
THIS TEXT WILL BECOME UPPERCASE AUTOMATICALLY.
LOGIN SUCCESSFUL
```

🖥 Console:
```
UppercaseDirective works — text converted to UPPERCASE
```

